```
// x[1]x[2]
// x[3]x[4] 00 01 11 10
// 00 | 1 | 0 | 0 | 1 |
// 01 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 |
// 11 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 |
// 10 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 1 |
```

From the K-map, we can identify the following groups of 1s:

1.  The four corners: x[3]'x[4]'x[1]'x[2]' + x[3]'x[4]'x[1]x[2]' + x[3]x[4]'x[1]'x[2]' + x[3]x[4]'x[1]x[2]' which simplifies to x[4]'x[2]'
2.  The group of four in the bottom left: x[3]x[4]x[1]'x[2]' + x[3]x[4]x[1]'x[2] + x[3]x[4]'x[1]'x[2]' + x[3]x[4]'x[1]'x[2] which simplifies to x[3]x[1]'
3.  The group of two in the bottom row: x[3]x[4]x[1]x[2]' + x[3]x[4]x[1]x[2] which simplifies to x[3]x[4]x[1]

Therefore, the minimized Boolean expression for `f` is:

f = (x[4]' & x[2]') | (x[3] & x[1]') | (x[3] & x[4] & x[1])

